---

<ArticleLayout
  title="IT Support Gold Coast — Managed IT for Small Business | BigByte Tech"
  description="Local IT support for Gold Coast small businesses — from Southport to Coolangatta. Fixed monthly fees, 24/7 response, cloud and security expertise. Free consultation."
  heading="IT Support for Gold Coast Small Businesses"
  intro="Managed IT support built for how Gold Coast businesses actually work — seasonal peaks, mobile teams and trading hours that don't stop at 5pm. Fixed monthly fees, 24/7 response."
  breadcrumb="IT Support Gold Coast"
  breadcrumbBase={{ label: "Services", href: "/#services" }}
  faqs={faqs}
  related={related}
>
  <p>
    Gold Coast businesses don't run on a nine-to-five schedule, and neither
    should their IT support. A booking system that crashes on a Saturday
    morning in peak season, EFTPOS dropping out during dinner service, or a
    site supervisor locked out of email at 6am — these aren't "log a ticket
    and we'll see you Monday" problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    BigByte Tech provides <strong>managed IT support across the Gold
    Coast</strong> — from Southport and Surfers Paradise down to Burleigh,
    Robina and Coolangatta — with a 24/7 rapid-response SLA and fixed monthly
    pricing. You get a full IT team watching your systems, for less than the
    cost of hiring one technician.
  </p>

  <h2>IT services we deliver on the Gold Coast</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Managed IT support</strong> — proactive monitoring, patching,
      unlimited helpdesk and on-site visits when needed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cyber security</strong> — a baseline built on the ACSC
      <a href="/guides/essential-eight-explained-small-business/"
        >Essential Eight</a
      >: multi-factor authentication, hardened devices, restricted admin
      access and tested backups.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloud migration and backup</strong> — Microsoft 365 setup and
      management, plus
      <a href="/guides/cloud-backup-vs-local-backup/"
        >backup strategies that survive ransomware</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business phone systems</strong> — modern
      <a href="/guides/voip-vs-landline-small-business-australia/"
        >VoIP phone systems</a
      > that follow your team between the office, home and the road.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Websites and automation</strong> — fast, SEO-ready business
      websites and workflow automation that cuts admin hours.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Built for the way Gold Coast businesses work</h2>

  <h3>Tourism and hospitality: your busiest day is everyone else's day off</h3>
  <p>
    School holidays, long weekends and event weeks are exactly when your
    booking platform, point-of-sale and Wi-Fi are under the most load — and
    when downtime costs the most. Our monitoring catches degrading systems
    before the rush, and our 24/7 response means a Saturday-night failure gets
    worked on Saturday night.
  </p>

  <h3>Trades and construction: your office is a ute</h3>
  <p>
    Quoting software, job management apps, shared plans and email all need to
    work from a phone or tablet on site at Coomera as reliably as they do at
    head office. We set up cloud systems and device management designed for
    teams that are rarely at a desk — and lock them down properly, because a
    lost phone shouldn't mean a data breach.
  </p>

  <h3>Professional and medical services: compliance isn't optional</h3>
  <p>
    Law firms, accountants, brokers and clinics handle exactly the data the
    Privacy Act and the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme care about. We build
    security and backup around those obligations, and document it — so when a
    client, insurer or regulator asks how their data is protected, you have a
    real answer.
  </p>

  <h2>Remote-first support, on-site when it matters</h2>
  <p>
    Around nine in ten issues are fixed faster remotely — we connect to the
    affected machine within minutes instead of driving the M1. That's better
    for you: shorter downtime and no call-out fees baked into your bill. For
    hardware failures, network and cabling work, office fit-outs and projects,
    we're on-site anywhere on the Coast. Being based in South East Queensland
    means we cover both
    <a href="/services/managed-it-support-brisbane/">Brisbane</a> and the Gold
    Coast with the same team and the same SLA.
  </p>

  <h2>Transparent fixed-fee pricing</h2>
  <p>
    One flat monthly fee per user covers monitoring, maintenance, security
    management and unlimited remote support. Projects are quoted separately
    and approved before any work starts. If you want to sanity-check our
    pricing against the market, read our honest guide to
    <a href="/guides/managed-it-support-cost-australia/"
      >what managed IT support costs in Australia</a
    > — we wrote it precisely because this industry loves hiding its prices.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Comparing providers?</strong> Take our
      <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-an-it-support-company/"
        >12 questions to ask an IT support company</a
      > into every sales meeting. The answers separate genuine partners from
      ticket factories.
    </p>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
